We need to understand the current client management feature. Let's look at the app/api/clients directory.

We already read app/api/clients/route.ts and app/api/clients/[id]/route.ts. These seem to be the API endpoints for client management.

The app/api/clients/route.ts handles GET requests for clients, with filtering by query and status.

The app/api/clients/[id]/route.ts handles GET, PATCH, and DELETE requests for a specific client.

We also read lib/clientRegistry.ts which contains the client registry logic, including functions to list clients, get client details, and manage remote access.

We also read lib/storage.ts which contains the storage layer for sites, orders, licenses, packages, etc.

We also read app/licenses/page.tsx which shows the current licenses page UI.

We also read app/pricing/page.tsx which shows the pricing page UI.

Now, we need to understand what the user wants:

1. Add complete client management feature like:
   - client order - edit, delete, payment status
   - license status with expired date
   - edit button click to see and edit the client all inputed full data
   - see his live site current health
   - purchased package info
   - license key
   - current slate core version
   - current active plugin list with remotely manage option like readonly or full access
   - re-Run bootstrap, Re-run setup button
   - etc

2. The frontend public page http://localhost:3000/pricing or the bookmarked page there also want edit and update your inputed data option for client so he can also edit his data if he put any wrong info.

So we need to:
1. Extend the existing client management API to support more fields and operations
2. Build a new admin client management UI (likely in the licenses page or a new page)
3. Add customer-facing order editing (likely in the pricing page or a new page)
4. Implement remote actions (like re-run bootstrap, re-run setup, remote access mode)
5. Add health monitoring and display

